# API routes — must come BEFORE the SPA fallback, or /* eats them.
# Kept here (instead of in netlify.toml) because Netlify's resolved order
# puts _redirects rules first and we need /api/* to win.
/api/*  /.netlify/functions/:splat  200

# WEC-303: SEO crawler endpoints. Same rationale — must come BEFORE the
# SPA fallback or Lighthouse + Googlebot get the index.html HTML when
# they ask for plain text/XML. Status 200 (not 301) so the served
# content is from the actual file at that path, not the redirect target.
/robots.txt   /robots.txt   200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200

# ─── TEMPORARY dev-host guard (re-instated 2026-09-22) ───────────────────
# A marketing campaign went out on 2026-09-17 with https://dev--fitpal-order
# .netlify.app instead of orders.fitpal.gr. Real customers placed real orders
# on the dev deploy, which is wired to the Viva DEMO merchant but to the SAME
# Supabase database — so sandbox payments wrote "paid" onto live orders and
# ~108 € was never actually collected.
#
# Timeline: added 17/09 · removed 22/09 to test WEC-819 (checkout form wiped
# on tab return on reseller storefronts, which needed a reachable dev host)
# · re-instated 22/09 once that test passed.
#
# Never ticketed. Earlier revisions of this block cited "WEC-790" — that is
# wrong, WEC-790 is the reseller zone time-slot half-ship. Don't chase it.
#
# Domain-level rule: the source is an absolute URL, so it matches ONLY that
# host. orders.fitpal.gr and localhost are untouched.
#
# Two carve-outs keep dev usable as a dev environment:
#   · /api/*   — already handled by the rule at the top of this file, which
#                matches on every host. Viva demo webhooks keep working.
#   · /order/* — the Viva demo success/failure return URLs registered in the
#                demo dashboard point here. Redirecting them would break the
#                dev payment flow.
#
# Developers: use the deploy permalink (<deploy-id>--fitpal-order.netlify.app),
# which is not the `dev--` host and is therefore not redirected. Removing this
# block is the only way to test on dev-- itself — do that deliberately, and
# put it back the same day.
#
# REMOVE THIS BLOCK once the campaign is cold.
https://dev--fitpal-order.netlify.app/order/*  /index.html  200
https://dev--fitpal-order.netlify.app/*  https://orders.fitpal.gr/:splat  302!
